{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0187KpP52tiQ47mZz66ZbPA3","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.0-uc003-nl\n     2→title: \"Number lines of files via nl\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go nl binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary numbers\n     6→  lines according to the active numbering style (body only by default), applying\n     7→  configurable format, width, separator, and start/increment values. The differential\n     8→  testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gnl\n     9→  from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are identical\n    10→  byte-for-byte.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd022-nl.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    16→  a passing differential test for cmd/nl.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs the Go nl binary on a file or stdin.\n    22→      Example: printf 'line one\\n\\nline three\\n' | ./bin/nl\n    23→  - id: F2\n    24→    step: |\n    25→      cmd/nl reads the input, recognizing section delimiter lines (\\\\:\\\\:\\\\:, \\\\:\\\\:, \\\\:)\n    26→      to identify header, body, and footer sections. All other lines are passed to the\n    27→      numbering logic.\n    28→  - id: F3\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      For each line in the current section, cmd/nl applies the section's numbering style\n    31→      (a/t/n/p RE). Lines selected for numbering receive a formatted line number prefix\n    32→      followed by the separator string and the line content.\n    33→  - id: F4\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/nl and gnl\n    36→      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    37→  - id: F5\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    40→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    41→  - id: F6\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    44→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    45→\n    46→touchpoints:\n    47→  - T1: \"cmd/nl — section parsing, line numbering, format/width/separator options (prd022-nl R1, R2, R3, R4)\"\n    48→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    49→\n    50→success_criteria:\n    51→  - id: S1\n    52→    criterion: cmd/nl compiles and ./bin/nl exists after mage build.\n    53→  - id: S2\n    54→    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; non-empty body lines are numbered in rn format at width 6 with tab separator.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: The differential test for -b a passes; all lines including empty lines are numbered.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: \"The differential test for -n ln -w 3 -s ': ' passes; format, width, and separator match gnl.\"\n    59→  - id: S5\n    60→    criterion: The differential test for -v 10 -i 5 passes; numbering starts at 10 and increments by 5.\n    61→  - id: S6\n    62→    criterion: The differential test for section delimiters with -h a passes; header lines are numbered and section delimiters are consumed without output.\n    63→\n    64→out_of_scope:\n    65→  - Regex numbering style (-b p RE) beyond basic pattern matching is not the primary test focus.\n    66→  - Locale-aware regex collation is not tested; LC_ALL=C is used throughout.\n    67→\n    68→test_suite: test-rel05.0\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73afb809-9fcb-49d3-bc09-5bbb3bc45bed","uuid":"05f71c26-ce9d-461b-880c-d87dcb366a75","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/348/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.0-uc003-nl.yaml","content":"id: rel05.0-uc003-nl\ntitle: \"Number lines of files via nl\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go nl binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary numbers\n  lines according to the active numbering style (body only by default), applying\n  configurable format, width, separator, and start/increment values. The differential\n  testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gnl\n  from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are identical\n  byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd022-nl.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/nl.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go nl binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: printf 'line one\\n\\nline three\\n' | ./bin/nl\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/nl reads the input, recognizing section delimiter lines (\\\\:\\\\:\\\\:, \\\\:\\\\:, \\\\:)\n      to identify header, body, and footer sections. All other lines are passed to the\n      numbering logic.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      For each line in the current section, cmd/nl applies the section's numbering style\n      (a/t/n/p RE). Lines selected for numbering receive a formatted line number prefix\n      followed by the separator string and the line content.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/nl and gnl\n      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/nl — section parsing, line numbering, format/width/separator options (prd022-nl R1, R2, R3, R4)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/nl compiles and ./bin/nl exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; non-empty body lines are numbered in rn format at width 6 with tab separator.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for -b a passes; all lines including empty lines are numbered.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: \"The differential test for -n ln -w 3 -s ': ' passes; format, width, and separator match gnl.\"\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for -v 10 -i 5 passes; numbering starts at 10 and increments by 5.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for section delimiters with -h a passes; header lines are numbered and section delimiters are consumed without output.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Regex numbering style (-b p RE) beyond basic pattern matching is not the primary test focus.\n  - Locale-aware regex collation is not tested; LC_ALL=C is used throughout.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.0\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
