{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LjGH8Mec8aARKiJ6Dk2du7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel05.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel05.0 — echo, tac, nl, fold\"\n     3→release: rel05.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel05.0-uc001-echo\n     7→  - rel05.0-uc002-tac\n     8→  - rel05.0-uc003-nl\n     9→  - rel05.0-uc004-fold\n    10→  - prd020-echo R1\n    11→  - prd020-echo R2\n    12→  - prd020-echo R3\n    13→  - prd021-tac R1\n    14→  - prd021-tac R2\n    15→  - prd021-tac R3\n    16→  - prd022-nl R1\n    17→  - prd022-nl R2\n    18→  - prd022-nl R3\n    19→  - prd022-nl R4\n    20→  - prd023-fold R1\n    21→  - prd023-fold R2\n    22→  - prd023-fold R3\n    23→\n    24→preconditions:\n    25→  - ./bin/echo, ./bin/tac, ./bin/nl, and ./bin/fold exist (built via mage build).\n    26→  - Reference binaries gecho, gtac, gnl, and gfold are installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n    27→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/echo/... ./cmd/tac/... ./cmd/nl/... ./cmd/fold/... which invoke RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    28→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    29→  - No normalization is applied; all outputs are compared byte-for-byte.\n    30→\n    31→test_cases:\n    32→\n    33→  # ---- echo ----\n    34→\n    35→  - name: echo_default_output\n    36→    description: No flags; arguments joined with spaces, followed by newline.\n    37→    inputs:\n    38→      args: [\"hello\", \"world\"]\n    39→      stdin: null\n    40→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    41→    normalization: none\n    42→    expected:\n    43→      exit_code: 0\n    44→      stdout: \"hello world\\n\"\n    45→      stderr: \"\"\n    46→    traces:\n    47→      - prd020-echo R1.1\n    48→\n    49→  - name: echo_no_args\n    50→    description: No arguments; outputs only a newline.\n    51→    inputs:\n    52→      args: []\n    53→      stdin: null\n    54→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    55→    normalization: none\n    56→    expected:\n    57→      exit_code: 0\n    58→      stdout: \"\\n\"\n    59→      stderr: \"\"\n    60→    traces:\n    61→      - prd020-echo R1.2\n    62→\n    63→  - name: echo_suppress_newline\n    64→    description: -n flag suppresses trailing newline.\n    65→    inputs:\n    66→      args: [\"-n\", \"hello\"]\n    67→      stdin: null\n    68→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    69→    normalization: none\n    70→    expected:\n    71→      exit_code: 0\n    72→      stdout: \"hello\"\n    73→      stderr: \"\"\n    74→    traces:\n    75→      - prd020-echo R1.3\n    76→\n    77→  - name: echo_escape_tab\n    78→    description: -e interprets \\\\t as a horizontal tab.\n    79→    inputs:\n    80→      args: [\"-e\", \"col1\\\\tcol2\"]\n    81→      stdin: null\n    82→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    83→    normalization: none\n    84→    expected:\n    85→      exit_code: 0\n    86→      stdout: \"col1\\tcol2\\n\"\n    87→      stderr: \"\"\n    88→    traces:\n    89→      - prd020-echo R2.1\n    90→\n    91→  - name: echo_escape_newline\n    92→    description: -e interprets \\\\n as an embedded newline.\n    93→    inputs:\n    94→      args: [\"-e\", \"line1\\\\nline2\"]\n    95→      stdin: null\n    96→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    97→    normalization: none\n    98→    expected:\n    99→      exit_code: 0\n   100→      stdout: \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n   101→      stderr: \"\"\n   102→    traces:\n   103→      - prd020-echo R2.1\n   104→\n   105→  - name: echo_escape_c_terminates\n   106→    description: -e with \\\\c terminates output at that point; no trailing newline.\n   107→    inputs:\n   108→      args: [\"-e\", \"before\\\\cafter\"]\n   109→      stdin: null\n   110→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   111→    normalization: none\n   112→    expected:\n   113→      exit_code: 0\n   114→      stdout: \"before\"\n   115→      stderr: \"\"\n   116→    traces:\n   117→      - prd020-echo R2.2\n   118→\n   119→  - name: echo_no_escape_default\n   120→    description: Without -e, backslash sequences are literal.\n   121→    inputs:\n   122→      args: [\"a\\\\tb\"]\n   123→      stdin: null\n   124→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   125→    normalization: none\n   126→    expected:\n   127→      exit_code: 0\n   128→      stdout: \"a\\\\tb\\n\"\n   129→      stderr: \"\"\n   130→    traces:\n   131→      - prd020-echo R2.3\n   132→\n   133→  - name: echo_combined_n_e\n   134→    description: -n -e combined; escape sequences processed and no trailing newline.\n   135→    inputs:\n   136→      args: [\"-n\", \"-e\", \"x\\\\ty\"]\n   137→      stdin: null\n   138→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   139→    normalization: none\n   140→    expected:\n   141→      exit_code: 0\n   142→      stdout: \"x\\ty\"\n   143→      stderr: \"\"\n   144→    traces:\n   145→      - prd020-echo R1.3\n   146→      - prd020-echo R2.1\n   147→\n   148→  # ---- tac ----\n   149→\n   150→  - name: tac_default_reversal\n   151→    description: Lines reversed; trailing newline preserved.\n   152→    inputs:\n   153→      args: []\n   154→      stdin: \"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\"\n   155→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   156→    normalization: none\n   157→    expected:\n   158→      exit_code: 0\n   159→      stdout: \"gamma\\nbeta\\nalpha\\n\"\n   160→      stderr: \"\"\n   161→    traces:\n   162→      - prd021-tac R1.1\n   163→      - prd021-tac R1.2\n   164→\n   165→  - name: tac_no_trailing_newline\n   166→    description: Input without trailing newline; last line (now first) has no newline.\n   167→    inputs:\n   168→      args: []\n   169→      stdin: \"a\\nb\\nc\"\n   170→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   171→    normalization: none\n   172→    expected:\n   173→      exit_code: 0\n   174→      stdout: \"c\\nb\\na\"\n   175→      stderr: \"\"\n   176→    traces:\n   177→      - prd021-tac R1.2\n   178→\n   179→  - name: tac_custom_separator\n   180→    description: -s ':' splits on colon; records reversed with colon separator after each.\n   181→    inputs:\n   182→      args: [\"-s\", \":\"]\n   183→      stdin: \"a:b:c:\"\n   184→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   185→    normalization: none\n   186→    expected:\n   187→      exit_code: 0\n   188→      stdout: \"c:b:a:\"\n   189→      stderr: \"\"\n   190→    traces:\n   191→      - prd021-tac R2.1\n   192→\n   193→  - name: tac_before_flag\n   194→    description: -b places separator before each record.\n   195→    inputs:\n   196→      args: [\"-b\", \"-s\", \":\"]\n   197→      stdin: \":a:b:c\"\n   198→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   199→    normalization: none\n   200→    expected:\n   201→      exit_code: 0\n   202→      stdout: \":c:b:a\"\n   203→      stderr: \"\"\n   204→    traces:\n   205→      - prd021-tac R2.2\n   206→\n   207→  - name: tac_single_line\n   208→    description: Single line input reverses to itself.\n   209→    inputs:\n   210→      args: []\n   211→      stdin: \"only\\n\"\n   212→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   213→    normalization: none\n   214→    expected:\n   215→      exit_code: 0\n   216→      stdout: \"only\\n\"\n   217→      stderr: \"\"\n   218→    traces:\n   219→      - prd021-tac R1.1\n   220→\n   221→  # ---- nl ----\n   222→\n   223→  - name: nl_default_body_numbering\n   224→    description: Default mode numbers non-empty body lines only; empty lines pass through unnumbered.\n   225→    inputs:\n   226→      args: []\n   227→      stdin: \"first\\n\\nsecond\\n\"\n   228→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   229→    normalization: none\n   230→    expected:\n   231→      exit_code: 0\n   232→      stdout: \"     1\\tfirst\\n\\n     2\\tsecond\\n\"\n   233→      stderr: \"\"\n   234→    traces:\n   235→      - prd022-nl R1.1\n   236→      - prd022-nl R1.2\n   237→\n   238→  - name: nl_number_all_lines\n   239→    description: -b a numbers every line including empty lines.\n   240→    inputs:\n   241→      args: [\"-b\", \"a\"]\n   242→      stdin: \"x\\n\\ny\\n\"\n   243→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   244→    normalization: none\n   245→    expected:\n   246→      exit_code: 0\n   247→      stdout: \"     1\\tx\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\ty\\n\"\n   248→      stderr: \"\"\n   249→    traces:\n   250→      - prd022-nl R2.1\n   251→\n   252→  - name: nl_format_ln_width_3_separator\n   253→    description: \"-n ln -w 3 -s ': ' uses left-justified 3-char field with custom separator.\"\n   254→    inputs:\n   255→      args: [\"-n\", \"ln\", \"-w\", \"3\", \"-s\", \": \"]\n   256→      stdin: \"a\\nb\\n\"\n   257→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   258→    normalization: none\n   259→    expected:\n   260→      exit_code: 0\n   261→      stdout: \"1  : a\\n2  : b\\n\"\n   262→      stderr: \"\"\n   263→    traces:\n   264→      - prd022-nl R3.1\n   265→      - prd022-nl R3.2\n   266→      - prd022-nl R3.3\n   267→\n   268→  - name: nl_start_and_increment\n   269→    description: -v 10 -i 5 starts at 10 and increments by 5.\n   270→    inputs:\n   271→      args: [\"-v\", \"10\", \"-i\", \"5\"]\n   272→      stdin: \"p\\nq\\nr\\n\"\n   273→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   274→    normalization: none\n   275→    expected:\n   276→      exit_code: 0\n   277→      stdout: \"    10\\tp\\n    15\\tq\\n    20\\tr\\n\"\n   278→      stderr: \"\"\n   279→    traces:\n   280→      - prd022-nl R3.4\n   281→\n   282→  - name: nl_section_delimiters\n   283→    description: Section delimiter lines consumed; header numbered with -h a.\n   284→    inputs:\n   285→      args: [\"-h\", \"a\"]\n   286→      stdin: \"\\\\:\\\\:\\\\:\\nheader line\\n\\\\:\\\\:\\nbody line\\n\"\n   287→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   288→    normalization: none\n   289→    expected:\n   290→      exit_code: 0\n   291→      stdout: \"     1\\theader line\\n     1\\tbody line\\n\"\n   292→      stderr: \"\"\n   293→    traces:\n   294→      - prd022-nl R4.1\n   295→      - prd022-nl R4.2\n   296→\n   297→  # ---- fold ----\n   298→\n   299→  - name: fold_default_width_80\n   300→    description: Lines up to 80 characters pass through unchanged.\n   301→    inputs:\n   302→      args: []\n   303→      stdin: \"short line\\n\"\n   304→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   305→    normalization: none\n   306→    expected:\n   307→      exit_code: 0\n   308→      stdout: \"short line\\n\"\n   309→      stderr: \"\"\n   310→    traces:\n   311→      - prd023-fold R1.2\n   312→\n   313→  - name: fold_wrap_at_width\n   314→    description: -w 4 wraps a 10-character string into segments of 4, 4, 2.\n   315→    inputs:\n   316→      args: [\"-w\", \"4\"]\n   317→      stdin: \"abcdefghij\"\n   318→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   319→    normalization: none\n   320→    expected:\n   321→      exit_code: 0\n   322→      stdout: \"abcd\\nefgh\\nij\"\n   323→      stderr: \"\"\n   324→    traces:\n   325→      - prd023-fold R1.1\n   326→      - prd023-fold R1.3\n   327→      - prd023-fold R1.4\n   328→\n   329→  - name: fold_space_break\n   330→    description: -w 11 -s breaks at the last space within 11 columns.\n   331→    inputs:\n   332→      args: [\"-w\", \"11\", \"-s\"]\n   333→      stdin: \"hello world foo\\n\"\n   334→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   335→    normalization: none\n   336→    expected:\n   337→      exit_code: 0\n   338→      stdout: \"hello world\\nfoo\\n\"\n   339→      stderr: \"\"\n   340→    traces:\n   341→      - prd023-fold R3.1\n   342→\n   343→  - name: fold_byte_mode\n   344→    description: -b measures width in bytes; no tab-stop expansion.\n   345→    inputs:\n   346→      args: [\"-b\", \"-w\", \"4\"]\n   347→      stdin: \"abcde\"\n   348→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   349→    normalization: none\n   350→    expected:\n   351→      exit_code: 0\n   352→      stdout: \"abcd\\ne\"\n   353→      stderr: \"\"\n   354→    traces:\n   355→      - prd023-fold R2.3\n   356→\n   357→  - name: fold_tab_columns\n   358→    description: Tab expands to tab stops for column counting; wrap accounts for tab width.\n   359→    inputs:\n   360→      args: [\"-w\", \"9\"]\n   361→      stdin: \"a\\tbcde\\n\"\n   362→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   363→    normalization: none\n   364→    expected:\n   365→      exit_code: 0\n   366→      stdout: \"a\\tbcd\\ne\\n\"\n   367→      stderr: \"\"\n   368→    traces:\n   369→      - prd023-fold R2.2\n   370→\n   371→  - name: fold_space_break_no_space\n   372→    description: -s with no space in first W columns falls back to hard wrap.\n   373→    inputs:\n   374→      args: [\"-w\", \"4\", \"-s\"]\n   375→      stdin: \"abcdefgh\\n\"\n   376→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   377→    normalization: none\n   378→    expected:\n   379→      exit_code: 0\n   380→      stdout: \"abcd\\nefgh\\n\"\n   381→      stderr: \"\"\n   382→    traces:\n   383→      - prd023-fold R3.2\n   384→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73afb809-9fcb-49d3-bc09-5bbb3bc45bed","uuid":"cabf7a1a-d8b8-40f7-9efe-d53f38f2c094","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/348/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel05.0.yaml","content":"id: test-rel05.0\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel05.0 — echo, tac, nl, fold\"\nrelease: rel05.0\n\ntraces:\n  - rel05.0-uc001-echo\n  - rel05.0-uc002-tac\n  - rel05.0-uc003-nl\n  - rel05.0-uc004-fold\n  - prd020-echo R1\n  - prd020-echo R2\n  - prd020-echo R3\n  - prd021-tac R1\n  - prd021-tac R2\n  - prd021-tac R3\n  - prd022-nl R1\n  - prd022-nl R2\n  - prd022-nl R3\n  - prd022-nl R4\n  - prd023-fold R1\n  - prd023-fold R2\n  - prd023-fold R3\n\npreconditions:\n  - ./bin/echo, ./bin/tac, ./bin/nl, and ./bin/fold exist (built via mage build).\n  - Reference binaries gecho, gtac, gnl, and gfold are installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/echo/... ./cmd/tac/... ./cmd/nl/... ./cmd/fold/... which invoke RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n  - No normalization is applied; all outputs are compared byte-for-byte.\n\ntest_cases:\n\n  # ---- echo ----\n\n  - name: echo_default_output\n    description: No flags; arguments joined with spaces, followed by newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"hello\", \"world\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"hello world\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R1.1\n\n  - name: echo_no_args\n    description: No arguments; outputs only a newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R1.2\n\n  - name: echo_suppress_newline\n    description: -n flag suppresses trailing newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-n\", \"hello\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"hello\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R1.3\n\n  - name: echo_escape_tab\n    description: -e interprets \\\\t as a horizontal tab.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-e\", \"col1\\\\tcol2\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"col1\\tcol2\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R2.1\n\n  - name: echo_escape_newline\n    description: -e interprets \\\\n as an embedded newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-e\", \"line1\\\\nline2\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"line1\\nline2\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R2.1\n\n  - name: echo_escape_c_terminates\n    description: -e with \\\\c terminates output at that point; no trailing newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-e\", \"before\\\\cafter\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"before\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R2.2\n\n  - name: echo_no_escape_default\n    description: Without -e, backslash sequences are literal.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"a\\\\tb\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"a\\\\tb\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R2.3\n\n  - name: echo_combined_n_e\n    description: -n -e combined; escape sequences processed and no trailing newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-n\", \"-e\", \"x\\\\ty\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"x\\ty\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd020-echo R1.3\n      - prd020-echo R2.1\n\n  # ---- tac ----\n\n  - name: tac_default_reversal\n    description: Lines reversed; trailing newline preserved.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"alpha\\nbeta\\ngamma\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"gamma\\nbeta\\nalpha\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd021-tac R1.1\n      - prd021-tac R1.2\n\n  - name: tac_no_trailing_newline\n    description: Input without trailing newline; last line (now first) has no newline.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"a\\nb\\nc\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"c\\nb\\na\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd021-tac R1.2\n\n  - name: tac_custom_separator\n    description: -s ':' splits on colon; records reversed with colon separator after each.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-s\", \":\"]\n      stdin: \"a:b:c:\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"c:b:a:\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd021-tac R2.1\n\n  - name: tac_before_flag\n    description: -b places separator before each record.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-b\", \"-s\", \":\"]\n      stdin: \":a:b:c\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \":c:b:a\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd021-tac R2.2\n\n  - name: tac_single_line\n    description: Single line input reverses to itself.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"only\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"only\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd021-tac R1.1\n\n  # ---- nl ----\n\n  - name: nl_default_body_numbering\n    description: Default mode numbers non-empty body lines only; empty lines pass through unnumbered.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"first\\n\\nsecond\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"     1\\tfirst\\n\\n     2\\tsecond\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd022-nl R1.1\n      - prd022-nl R1.2\n\n  - name: nl_number_all_lines\n    description: -b a numbers every line including empty lines.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-b\", \"a\"]\n      stdin: \"x\\n\\ny\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"     1\\tx\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\ty\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd022-nl R2.1\n\n  - name: nl_format_ln_width_3_separator\n    description: \"-n ln -w 3 -s ': ' uses left-justified 3-char field with custom separator.\"\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-n\", \"ln\", \"-w\", \"3\", \"-s\", \": \"]\n      stdin: \"a\\nb\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"1  : a\\n2  : b\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd022-nl R3.1\n      - prd022-nl R3.2\n      - prd022-nl R3.3\n\n  - name: nl_start_and_increment\n    description: -v 10 -i 5 starts at 10 and increments by 5.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-v\", \"10\", \"-i\", \"5\"]\n      stdin: \"p\\nq\\nr\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"    10\\tp\\n    15\\tq\\n    20\\tr\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd022-nl R3.4\n\n  - name: nl_section_delimiters\n    description: Section delimiter lines consumed; header numbered with -h a.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-h\", \"a\"]\n      stdin: \"\\\\:\\\\:\\\\:\\nheader line\\n\\\\:\\\\:\\nbody line\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"     1\\theader line\\n     1\\tbody line\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd022-nl R4.1\n      - prd022-nl R4.2\n\n  # ---- fold ----\n\n  - name: fold_default_width_80\n    description: Lines up to 80 characters pass through unchanged.\n    inputs:\n      args: []\n      stdin: \"short line\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"short line\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd023-fold R1.2\n\n  - name: fold_wrap_at_width\n    description: -w 4 wraps a 10-character string into segments of 4, 4, 2.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-w\", \"4\"]\n      stdin: \"abcdefghij\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"abcd\\nefgh\\nij\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd023-fold R1.1\n      - prd023-fold R1.3\n      - prd023-fold R1.4\n\n  - name: fold_space_break\n    description: -w 11 -s breaks at the last space within 11 columns.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-w\", \"11\", \"-s\"]\n      stdin: \"hello world foo\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"hello world\\nfoo\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd023-fold R3.1\n\n  - name: fold_byte_mode\n    description: -b measures width in bytes; no tab-stop expansion.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-b\", \"-w\", \"4\"]\n      stdin: \"abcde\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"abcd\\ne\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd023-fold R2.3\n\n  - name: fold_tab_columns\n    description: Tab expands to tab stops for column counting; wrap accounts for tab width.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-w\", \"9\"]\n      stdin: \"a\\tbcde\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"a\\tbcd\\ne\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd023-fold R2.2\n\n  - name: fold_space_break_no_space\n    description: -s with no space in first W columns falls back to hard wrap.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-w\", \"4\", \"-s\"]\n      stdin: \"abcdefgh\\n\"\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"abcd\\nefgh\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd023-fold R3.2\n","numLines":384,"startLine":1,"totalLines":384}}}
